Sergeant Ulrich Benda is a human soldier of a company from beyond the firmament, one of the crew that raised and ran [[Geography/Hesperid 3|Hesperid 3]]. He wore a blue, tailored uniform with his name on a tag, and the company marks its works and its people with a small triangle of sixteen dots.

His voice was left in the works' consoles as a running log. He told how the company got its start, after its founders met a ship full of shipwrecked people in the Far Realms, and how he and his own crew had ended up shipwrecked in turn. He waited on a shipment home to the company's ship, the [[Geography/Hesperid|Hesperid]], which the company called HQ, and went years without an answer from it. His last entries record Sybil's death and his and Thurston's turn away from HQ's protocol, and he signs off saying the two of them escaped the place.
